From 84f64df8918beebfb479252c2eb098f1a889204a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:28:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fog): apply native biome and command settings

Accept resolved fog snapshots through a connection-owned receiver. Select
the camera's received biome key from the snapshot, below command settings
and above the existing core default policy. Apply fixed and render-relative
air distances and colors through the atmospheric pipeline, preserving later
camera, vision and void modifiers and existing fluid/weather paths.

Retire state on disconnect or listener replacement and reject callbacks
from older generations. Removing the final command reveals the selected
biome instead of Java's 1,024-block distance and purple End sky. The native
qualified End-biome fixture supplies the fixed 0..32 red control.

Matching native 1.26.60.5 uniforms establish the living admitted End dragon
cap at 0..min(100, effective render distance), with or without commands.
Retain that override above the resolved air distances, preserve colors and
restore ordinary settings after death. Boss bars do not own actor lifetime.

Render End skies with the licensed world-selected grayscale texture and
native color multiplication, below server overrides. Decode off-thread and
upload during client ticks before render passes. Dispatch disconnect GPU
retirement to the client executor and check listener ownership inside the
task so an old disconnect cannot clear a replacement session.

Focused regressions cover resource/session retirement, empty commands,
medium boundaries and the observed dragon cap. Spatial biome blending,
legacy default bindings, engine-specific vanilla rules, exact transitions,
End sky motion/sampling, fluids and weather still need native comparisons.

BREAKING CHANGE: The fog receiver requires the matching core payload version 2.
